# Global git ignore ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore).
# Git reads this in EVERY repo automatically (no core.excludesFile needed), and
# ripgrep (rg) + fd honor it too -- so code searches skip these regenerable
# trees in any directory, layered on top of each repo's own .gitignore.
#
# Conservative on purpose: only ALWAYS-junk dirs live here. build/ and dist/ are
# deliberately excluded -- they're real source-dir names in some projects, and a
# global ignore also hides untracked files from `git status` everywhere. Leave
# those to per-repo .gitignore.

# --- existing project patterns (do not remove) ---
**/.claude/settings.local.json

**/.claude/.cc-writes/

# --- regenerable build / dependency / cache trees ---
node_modules/
target/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
